      "finding": {
        "id": "C-38",
        "reviewer": "review-highload",
        "severity": "info",
        "file": "src/remote/client.ts",
        "line": 459,
        "quote": "      approvalId = id;\n    } catch {\n      return { decision: \"deny\", undelivered: true };",
        "problem": "client.askApproval edge cases: the catch around POST plus response.json() marks a lost response as undelivered (false positive), a post-POST disconnect returns deny with no undelivered flag and leaves the topic card open (false negative), RemoteBridge does not set the flag on throw, and raceApproval can accept a late topic press just before settled is set.",
        "impact": "Failure mode: after a slow bridge response the operator sees 'mirror not delivered' in the TUI but may still press the Telegram card; that press finds no waiter and is dropped, so it is harmless to state (fail-closed) but the note is wrong in that window. A cosmetic mislabel, not a data-integrity issue.",
        "suggested_fix": "Mark undelivered: true only when the failure is known to precede the request being accepted (not connected, non-ok response, missing id); for a thrown error after send, either omit the flag or word the note as 'delivery unconfirmed'.",
        "evidence": "src/remote/client.ts lines 450-462: one catch for post(), response.ok, and json() failures, returning undelivered: true. Also reported by: review-highload-w3:F-004, review-highload-w3:F-002, review-logic-w3:F-004, review-logic-w3:F-005.",
        "confidence": "low"
      },
      "claimed_disposition": "fixed"
    },
    {
      "round": 1,
      "finding": {
        "id": "C-42",
        "reviewer": "review-highload",
        "severity": "info",
        "file": "src/commands/operator-confirm-tools.ts",
        "line": 192,
        "quote": "pending.set(token, {",
        "problem": "Pre-existing: entries in the process-local pending token map are removed only by invoke or confirmationDeclined; abandoned cards are never swept (the PR adds issuedAt but no eviction).",
        "impact": "One small object per abandoned card. A single operator shell asks a handful of cards a day, so growth is negligible. It is a leak only in a shell that runs for months with many abandoned cards.",
        "suggested_fix": "Optional: on each `confirmation()` call, drop entries older than REMOTE_CARD_TTL_MS, using the `issuedAt` this PR already stores.",
        "evidence": "src/commands/operator-confirm-tools.ts: `pending.set(token, { input: key(input), card, shown, prepared: built.prepared, issuedAt: now().getTime() })` at line 192. The 1-hour TTL is checked only inside invoke for remote answers, and no timer or sweep exists. The Map and its set/delete pattern pre-date this PR; the PR only adds `issuedAt`. Also reported by: review-logic-w2:F-003, review-performance-w2:F-002.",
        "confidence": "high"
      },
      "claimed_disposition": "fixed"
    }
  ],
